# Six Sines for WebCLAP

Six Sines by BaconPaul (Paul Walker), a synthesizer with audio rate modulation, ported to WebCLAP. This is not an
official Six Sines release.

- Six Sines: https://github.com/baconpaul/six-sines (commit 03f3b9a)
- This port, and the complete source of this bundle: @SOURCE_URL@
  Build it with `scripts/build-six-sines.sh`, which fetches every dependency below at the commit named here.

## License

The bundle as a whole is licensed under the **GNU Affero General Public License, version 3** (`LICENSE`).

- `module.wasm` (the synthesizer) is GPL-3.0 (`licenses/GPL-3.0.txt`). Six Sines' own source is MIT, its
  dependencies sst-basic-blocks and sst-filters are GPL-3.0, so the combined work is GPL-3.0, as upstream
  states.
- `ui/ui.wasm` (the editor) also contains the JUCE framework, used under the AGPL-3.0, so it is AGPL-3.0.
  GPL-3.0 section 13 permits the combination.

This program is distributed in the hope that it will be useful, but WITHOUT ANY WARRANTY; without even the implied
warranty of MERCHANTABILITY or FITNESS FOR A PARTICULAR PURPOSE. See the licenses for details.

